.TH DRAGONGL-SERVER 1 "2026-09-06" "DragonGL 2026.09.04.02" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dragongl-server \- Dragon GL server launcher script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dragongl-server
.RI "[\-\-password\ |\ -p\ " pwd ]
.RI "[\-\-dm\-password\ |\ -d\ " pwd ]"
.RI "[\-\-port\ |\ -P\ " port ]"
.RI "[\-\-help\ |\ -h ]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dragongl-server
is a convenience launcher for the Dragon GL master server. Before starting
the server it prints diagnostic information about the host (operating
system, uptime and load, memory usage, disk space, network interfaces) and
then executes
.B build/dragongl_server
from the project root directory, passing the selected options.

NOTE: the diagnostics block prints the machine's IP addresses to the log;
set
.B DIAGNOSTICS=0
in the environment to skip it.

The access password is mandatory: if no option is given, the script prints
an error and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-password " pwd"
Set the server access password (required).
.TP
.BI \-d ", " \-\-dm\-password " pwd"
Set the dedicated password of the privileged
.B dm
account (see
.BR dragongl_server (1)).
.TP
.BI \-P ", " \-\-port " port"
TCP port to listen on (default 8080).
.TP
.B \-h , \-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the server with a custom password:
.PP
.RS
.B dragongl-server --password segreto123
.RE
.PP
Start a second server on another port with a dedicated DM password:
.PP
.RS
.B dragongl-server --password segreto123 --dm-password dm123 --port 9000
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dragongl_server (1),
.BR dragongl-client (1)
